      "side": 1,
      "message": "`allow`, `warn` and `deny` become new `define-library` declarations, which another R7RS implementation will reject. A portable library can still write `(cond-expand (vali (allow platform-features)))`. That\u0027s worth saying here, and under ADR 0021 a `cond-expand` on `vali` is a build identifier, so it doesn\u0027t affect portability.\n\nConsider also one form, such as `(lint (allow platform-features))`, instead of three declaration keywords. It claims one name in the declaration namespace instead of three, and leaves room for groups later (Left open).",
      "revId": "a61eb46e833ac8ec757db88b129eaf13cdc9bdb2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
