      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T13:49:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should the artifact store findings before levels are applied? If it stores what was reported, then a lint at `allow` when the artifact was built leaves nothing to replay. Raising it later, with item 6\u0027s flag or a project configuration (item 7), shows nothing on a cache hit, but shows it on a cold build. That\u0027s the cold/hot difference this item is meant to prevent.\n\nStoring every finding with its lint name, and applying levels (declarations, flags, configuration) when reporting, keeps the two the same. It also means changing a level never needs a rebuild.\n\nRelated: replaying every imported library\u0027s warnings on each compile of a program that uses them gets noisy, for warnings nobody building the program can act on. rustc caps lints from dependencies (`--cap-lints`). The open question about `deny` across imports (Left open) probably wants the same answer: report at full level for the libraries being built, and cap for the rest.",
      "revId": "a61eb46e833ac8ec757db88b129eaf13cdc9bdb2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
